    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48762" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">transcursĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				passing over</i>, <i>lapse</i> of a period of
			time (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">decennii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 6, 23, 27 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A hasty treatment</i>, <i>brief
				handling</i> in thought: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non perfunctoria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Psa. 118</span></i>
			, Serm, 13, 7 <i>init.</i></div>
